    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d651">

                <pb facs="0620" n="536" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg536"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860c.48/141</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-04T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 4, 1918, noon</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 5, 11.33
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5036. Department’s 2758, September 20, 6 p.m. Swiss Government shows great
                    interest and desires to cooperate and has asked German Government for all
                    guarantees outlined. Difficulty is, however, foreseen as to destruction of tin
                    containers. Please inform me whether it is not practicable to ship the milk in
                    paper containers such as I understand are prescribed by New Jersey law.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
